---
import Prose from '../../layouts/Prose.astro';
import Capture from '../../components/Capture.astro';
import Chord from '../../components/Chord.astro';
import { getDocsPage } from '../../data/docs-topics';

const page = getDocsPage('markdown');
---
<Prose title={page.title} description={page.description} path={page.path}>
  <Capture name="markdown-inline" alt="A Markdown file in Inline mode: headings, a list and checkboxes formatted, the line being edited showing its markup" />
  <p>A Markdown file opens in Inline mode: headings, emphasis, lists, checkboxes, links, images and code blocks are formatted where they are written, and the line you are editing shows its markup. Source shows the plain text. The status bar switches between the two, and so does <Chord of="CmdOrCtrl+Shift+V" />; Settings, Editor, Markdown opens in sets which one a Markdown file opens in. Tables, math and Mermaid diagrams are drawn in place, and each shows its source while the cursor is in it. A Markdown file over 5 MB opens in large-file mode, without Inline formatting.</p>
  <p>Lists continue on <Chord of="Enter" />, a checkbox toggles on click, and <Chord of="CmdOrCtrl+B" />, <Chord of="CmdOrCtrl+I" />, <Chord of="CmdOrCtrl+K" /> wrap the selection. In a Markdown file, <code>[[File]]</code> opens that file, <code>[[Folder/File]]</code> picks one of two with the same name, and <code>[[File#Heading]]</code> opens it at the heading. Typing <code>[[</code> offers the files in the folder. Renaming a file offers to update the links that point at it.</p>
  <p>Pasting an image or a copied image file into a Markdown file, or dropping image files on it, inserts an image link at the cursor or the drop point, and one undo removes it. A pasted screenshot is saved as a PNG named after the file and the time. A copied or dropped image already inside the file's folder is linked where it is; any other is copied in, and a file with the same name gets a number unless it holds the same image. Images go to an <code>assets</code> folder beside the Markdown file; Settings, General, Image folder changes it, and an empty value saves them beside the file. Each image must be a PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, BMP, AVIF or SVG file of 16 MB or less. Dropping other files opens them as tabs.</p>
  <p>An image from a web address shows its host and a Load image button until you click it. Settings, Editor, Load web images loads them without asking, except an image on this computer or the local network. Web images are fetched over https; an image on a device on your own network can be loaded over http when you click.</p>
</Prose>
